> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No database migrations needed** — the existing schema already has all required columns (`predicted_sales_next_week`, `predicted_sales_next_month`, `restock_recommendation`, `optimal_price`, `price_elasticity`, `next_purchase_probability`, `predicted_days_to_next_purchase`, `confidence_score`, `accuracy_score`, `favorite_brands`).

> [!NOTE]
> All AI algorithms are implemented in **pure PHP** — no external libraries (Python, scikit-learn, etc.) required. This keeps deployment simple for the graduation project.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests

Run the existing Artisan commands to verify the AI system processes data correctly:

```bash
# 1. Update all analytics (runs customer + product analytics with new AI algorithms)
php artisan analytics:update

# 2. Generate sales predictions (runs Exponential Smoothing + Linear Regression)
php artisan analytics:predict --days=7 --period=day

# 3. Detect patterns (runs Z-Score anomaly detection)
php artisan analytics:detect-patterns
```

### Manual Verification

1. After running `analytics:update`, check `customer_analytics` table and verify:
   - `customer_segment` values change dynamically based on RFM clustering
   - `next_purchase_probability` is calculated (not 0)
   - `predicted_days_to_next_purchase` is calculated
   - `favorite_brands` is populated

2. After running `analytics:predict`, check `sales_predictions` table and verify:
   - `confidence_score` varies (not just 30/50/70/90)
   - `model_version` shows the AI algorithm name

3. Test API endpoints via Postman/curl:
   - `GET /api/analytics/dashboard` — should return AI metadata
   - `GET /api/analytics/recommendations/me` — should return collaborative filtering results
   - `GET /api/analytics/alerts` — should show anomaly-based alerts
